{
  "version": "schemaxis.readiness/1",
  "routes": {
    "schemaxis.ngspice/1": {
      "guide": "docs/ngspice.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Analyse bounded ideal linear networks: DC voltages, linear/decade/octave AC frequency response, input impedance/current/power, passive branch current/power, and first-order RC charging. Named finite-sample voltage, gain, relative phase, current, power and impedance requirements gate publication.",
        "assumptions": "Qualified ngspice-47 executable in an isolated process with startup files disabled. SI volts, ohms, farads, henries, Hz and seconds. One ideal voltage source to ground node 0. The node name gnd is reserved in any case because ngspice rewrites it to node 0. AC phasors use exp(+j*omega*t). AC amplitudeConvention declares peak (default; power factor 1/2) or rms (power factor 1). Source input current is native -i(vdrive), independently checked against KCL; branch currents and powers derive from verified native terminal voltages.",
        "constraints": "At most sixteen non-ground nodes, 64 resistors, 64 capacitors, 64 AC-only uncoupled inductors and 512 actual samples. Every node needs a resistor/inductor path to ground or the driven node. No ideal-inductor loops or inductive shorts across the source. No arbitrary netlists, models, semiconductors, mutual coupling, imported KiCad projects, inductor DC sweeps or general transient networks. rcStep is exactly series R and shunt C, initially uncharged, over 0.01–20 RC time constants. AC requires at least three points and at most fifteen selected probes within the shared 64-column table limit. Every requested frequency must have a nonsingular, sufficiently conditioned nodal system. Requirements inspect declared samples only; no continuous operating-envelope or all-component-tolerance guarantee. Phase acceptance uses relative output/source principal phase in [-180,180] degrees and refuses zero response. Logarithmic points is nominal samples per decade/octave; actual count must be 3–512. Selected outputs together must fit 64 numeric columns. portMetrics refuses undefined or numerically ill-conditioned input impedance near zero current.",
        "inspection": "Inspect results.csv for selected voltages and AC real/imaginary/magnitude/phase columns. circuit-summary.json retains topology, units, first/last sample and independent maximum voltage discrepancy. circuit.cir is the generated inspectable netlist. Named requirements retain minimum/maximum native observations, signed bound margins and worst sample coordinates. AC branchProbes add derived current phasors and passive active/reactive power. portMetrics adds native-observed input current, derived input impedance and complex/apparent power; amplitudeConvention and complexPowerFactor are retained. frequencyGrid records spacing and actual sample count.",
        "recovery": "INVALID_CIRCUIT at a node named gnd (any case) needs 0 for ground or another node name: ngspice rewrites gnd to node 0, so the reserved alias is refused rather than normalised. FLOATING_CIRCUIT needs a resistor/inductor reference path. INVALID_SWEEP needs stop > start. ILL_CONDITIONED_CIRCUIT needs damping or bounded component ratios. UNSUPPORTED_CIRCUIT requires the first-order RC topology for rcStep or removal of an ideal-inductor/source loop for AC. Configure ngspice-47 for INTERPRETER_NOT_FOUND; retain native logs and correct the input before a fresh attempt. INVALID_REQUIREMENT needs a supported quantity/probe and an ordered sample-containing window. PERFORMANCE_NOT_MET needs review of the worst condition, circuit/excitation or authored bounds, then a fresh attempt; this is distinct from native/physics failure. UNDEFINED_OBSERVABLE needs nonzero measured response for phase/dB, or a physical input load/disabled portMetrics for input impedance. RESOURCE_LIMIT at circuit needs fewer published probes."
      },
